  "summary": "BTR_CLI is a research PoC that weaponizes Microsoft's signed Windows Defender Boot-Time Removal driver (BTR.sys) as an arbitrary file/registry kernel primitive by forging its RC4-encrypted, ~CRC32-validated transaction config stored in a :changelist ADS. The driver is staged as a SERVICE_SYSTEM_START (Start=1) service in the \"Boot Bus Extender\" group, executing in a pre-EDR \"Golden Window\" after the filesystem is writable but before user-mode AV services start. Detection relies on ADS creation on .sys files, System (PID 4) file/registry operations after a driver load, and non-Defender process lineage for the driver.",
